      "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\n### Summary\nThe createMarket() function cannot atomically update Pyth oracle price feeds before market initialization, causing market creation to systematically fail for volatile assets (ETH, BTC, MON) when the cached Pyth price exceeds the staleness threshold (typically 10 minutes). This directly contradicts the protocol's documented design where \"volatile assets (e.g., ETH, BTC, MON) are priced through pull feeds from Pyth\" (from audit README).\n\n## Root Cause Analysis\n\nRoot Cause Analysis\nThe vulnerability exists in the createMarket() execution flow:\n1. Entry Point - Covenant.sol \n```solidity\nfunction createMarket(\n    MarketParams calldata marketParams,\n    bytes calldata initData  //  Only contains market config, NOT oracle update data\n) external noDelegateCall returns (MarketId) {  // NOT payable - cannot send ETH for Pyth fees\n    \n    MarketId marketId = marketParams.id();\n    ValidationLogic.checkMarketParams(marketParams, idToMarketParams[marketId], isLexEnabled, isCuratorEnabled);\n\n    //   Directly calls initMarket WITHOUT updating oracle price\n    (SynthTokens memory synthTokens, bytes memory lexData) = \n        ILiquidExchangeModel(marketParams.lex).initMarket(\n            marketId,\n            marketParams,\n            _defaultProtocolFee,\n            initData  // This is market configuration data, NOT oracle update data\n        );\n    \n    idToMarketParams[marketId] = marketParams;\n    marketState[marketId].authorizedPauseAddress = _defaultPauseAddress;\n    marketState[marketId].statusFlag = STATE_UNLOCKED;\n\n    emit Events.CreateMarket(marketId, marketParams, synthTokens, initData, lexData);\n    return marketId;\n}\nIssues:\n\nFunction is NOT payable → Cannot send ETH to pay Pyth update fees\ninitData parameter is for market configuration → NOT oracle price update data\nNo call to updatePriceFeeds() before reading prices\n\n2. Market Initialization - LatentSwapLEX.sol \n\nfunction initMarket(\n    MarketId marketId,\n    MarketParams calldata marketParams,\n    uint32 protocolFee,\n    bytes calldata initData  // Market config only\n) external onlyCovenantCore returns (SynthTokens memory synthTokens, bytes memory lexData) {\n    \n    // ... token creation logic ...\n    \n    //   Reads price WITHOUT updating oracle first \n    (uint256 currentBasePrice, ) = LatentSwapLogic.readBasePriceAndCalculateLiqRatio(\n        marketParams,\n        _targetXvsL,\n        int8(info.quoteDecimals) - int8(info.synthDecimals),\n        false  //  isPreview = FALSE enforces STRICT staleness check\n    );\n    \n    // ... initialize market state ...\n}\nIssues:\n\nNo _updateOraclePrice() call before reading price\nUses isPreview = false which enforces strict staleness checks\n\n3. Price Reading - LatentSwapLogic.sol\nfunction readBasePriceAndCalculateLiqRatio(\n    MarketParams calldata marketParams,\n    uint256 liquidityConcentrationX96,\n    int8 scaleDecimals,\n    bool isPreview\n) external view returns (uint256 price, uint256 liqRatioX96) {\n    return _readBasePriceAndCalculateLiqRatio(\n        marketParams, liquidityConcentrationX96, scaleDecimals, isPreview\n    );\n}\n\nfunction _readBasePriceAndCalculateLiqRatio(\n    MarketParams calldata marketParams,\n    uint256 targetXvsL,\n    int8 scaleDecimals,\n    bool isPreview\n) internal view returns (uint256 price, uint256 liqRatioX96) {\n    \n    //  When isPreview=false, uses getQuote() with STRICT staleness\n    liqRatioX96 = (isPreview)\n        ? IPriceOracle(marketParams.curator).previewGetQuote(...)  // Lenient\n        : IPriceOracle(marketParams.curator).getQuote(...);         // ← STRICT (used in createMarket!)\n    \n    // ... calculations ...\n}\nIssues:\n\nisPreview = false triggers strict staleness check via getQuote()\nPyth oracle will revert if price is >10 minutes stale\n\n4. Pyth Oracle Enforcement - PythOracle.sol\n```solidity\nfunction _fetchPriceStruct() internal view returns (PythStructs.Price memory) {\n    PythStructs.Price memory p = IPyth(pyth).getPriceUnsafe(feedId);\n\n    if (p.publishTime < block.timestamp) {\n        uint256 staleness = block.timestamp - p.publishTime;\n        if (staleness > maxStaleness) {\n            revert Errors.PriceOracle_InvalidAnswer();  //  REVERTS if stale\n        }\n    }\n    // ...\n}\n```\n## Attack Scenario / User Impact\n\nUser wants to create ETH/USDC market using Pyth oracle\nPyth's cached ETH price is 11 minutes old (normal during low activity)\nUser calls createMarket(marketParams, initData)\nExecution path: createMarket() → initMarket() → readBasePriceAndCalculateLiqRatio() → getQuote()\nPythOracle checks: staleness = 11 minutes > maxStaleness (10 minutes)\nTransaction REVERTS with PriceOracle_InvalidAnswer\nUser must now:\n\nCall curator.updatePriceFeeds{value: fee}() separately\nImmediately call createMarket() before price goes stale again\nHope no one else creates the market first (race condition)\nPay double gas costs\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n```solidity\nfunction createMarket(\n    MarketParams calldata marketParams,\n    bytes calldata initData,\n    bytes calldata oracleUpdateData  //  ADD: Oracle update data\n) external payable noDelegateCall returns (MarketId) {  //  ADD: payable modifier\n    \n    MarketId marketId = marketParams.id();\n    ValidationLogic.checkMarketParams(marketParams, idToMarketParams[marketId], isLexEnabled, isCuratorEnabled);\n\n    // ADD: Update oracle price before market initialization\n    if (oracleUpdateData.length > 0) {\n        IPriceOracle(marketParams.curator).updatePriceFeeds{value: msg.value}(\n            marketParams.baseToken,\n            marketParams.quoteToken,\n            oracleUpdateData\n        );\n    } else if (msg.value > 0) {\n        revert Errors.Covenant_Overdeposit();\n    }\n\n    (SynthTokens memory synthTokens, bytes memory lexData) = \n        ILiquidExchangeModel(marketParams.lex).initMarket(\n            marketId,\n            marketParams,\n            _defaultProtocolFee,\n            initData\n        );\n    \n    // ... rest of function\n}\n```",
